<title>JAPAN: Japan trust banks see higher operating profits.</title>
<headline>Japan trust banks see higher operating profits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seven trust banks made the following forecasts for parent operating profits for the business year ending March 31, 1997. (In billions of yen, with actual profits for 1995/96).</p>
<p>				    1996/97	   1995/1996</p>
<p> Mitsui		 80		    67.3</p>
<p> Mitsubishi	  360		   204.3</p>
<p> Sumitomo	    360		   182.5</p>
<p> Yasuda		140		   107.3</p>
<p> Nippon		 14		     7.1</p>
<p> Toyo		  135		    47.9</p>
<p> Chuo		   85		    36.6</p>
<p> Total			  1,174		   653.0</p>
<p>The full names of the banks are Mitsu Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd, Mitsubishi Trust &amp; Banking Corp, Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd, Yasuda Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd, Nippon Trust Bank Ltd, Toyo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd and Chuo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
